  "as_of": "2023-05-25",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would continue the Australia Council as Creative Australia, with expanded responsibilities and a revised governing board for the national arts funding body.",
   "It would establish Music Australia to support contemporary music and Creative Workplaces to promote fair, safe and respectful conditions for artists and arts workers.",
   "Both new parts would operate within Creative Australia under board oversight, alongside a companion bill dealing with repeal of the former legislation and transitional matters."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "The governing Australia Council Board would expand to a maximum of fourteen members.",
   "Board appointments could last four years, with total service limited to nine years.",
   "Separate councils would advise the board on Music Australia and Creative Workplaces.",
   "The chief executive would chair the music council but could not chair the workplace council."
  ],
  "affected": "Australian artists, contemporary musicians, arts workers, arts organisations and Creative Australia's governing bodies are affected.",
